## Why This Is Asked
This question blends BFS reachability, Dijkstra shortest paths, and counting shortest paths via a DAG and topological order.

## Key Concepts
- BFS/DFS reachability
- Dijkstra's algorithm
- Shortest-path DAG
- Topological DP and modular counting

## Code Example
```javascript
function countShortestPaths(n, adj, s) {
  const dist = Array(n).fill(Infinity); dist[s] = 0;
  // priority queue based Dijkstra (pseudo-notation)
  const pq = new MinPQ((a,b)=>a[0]-b[0]);
  pq.enqueue([0,s]);
  while(!pq.isEmpty()){
    const [d,u] = pq.dequeue(); if (d!==dist[u]) continue;
    for (const {to:v, w} of adj[u]){
      if (dist[v] > d + w){ dist[v] = d + w; pq.enqueue([dist[v], v]); }
    }
  }
  const dag = Array.from({length:n}, ()=>[]);
  for (let u=0; u<n; u++) for (const {to:v, w} of adj[u]) if (dist[u] + w === dist[v]) dag[u].push(v);
  const order = Array.from({length:n}, (_,i)=>i).sort((a,b)=>dist[a]-dist[b]);
  const MOD = 1000000007; const ways = Array(n).fill(0); ways[s] = 1;
  for (const u of order) for (const v of dag[u]) ways[v] = (ways[v] + ways[u]) % MOD;
  return {dist, ways};
}
```

